    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Plastic Waste:
- Complete the upgrading recycling systems in Lebanese industries to enhance recovery and recycling capacity of plastics within Lebanon: 
GPI: recycling capacity of 1000 kg / hr of post Consumer PET Bottles and Containers (for 6000 tons a year; approx. 100 Million Bottles). 
Masterpak: recycling capacity of 600 kg / hr. of post Consumer and post commercial PP/ PE/ LDPE Plastic materials (for a maximum capacity of 300 tons/month) 
- Conduct field visits to the 2 industries, 
- Conduct inauguration event at the end of the project. 
- Prepare and disseminate infographics showing the results of the plastic study and benefits of a circular economy 

E-Waste: 
- Complete the analysis of the survey on e-waste and assessment of the results. 
- Working with UNU on the integration of the data on e-waste statistics toolkit, in order finalize the national e-waste assessment 
- Development of the recommendation report on how Lebanon can manage the e-waste. 

- Implementation phase: complete the technical support for the 2 beneficiaries:
Ecoserv: provide the needed equipment to enhance the e-waste collection through the NGO drop-off zones
Verdetech: improving their management system in order to improve their performance 

Stabilization Through Solid Waste Projects in Lebanon (Nafakhieh)
- Two technical analysis reports undertaken (including design and tender documents for landfill in Nafakhieh)
- Recruit project staff
- launching of bid for construction works</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Plastic Waste:
- Complete the upgrading recycling systems in Lebanese industries to enhance recovery and recycling capacity of plastics within Lebanon: 
GPI: recycling capacity of 1000 kg / hr of post Consumer PET Bottles and Containers (for 6000 tons a year; approx. 100 Million Bottles).  
3MPlast: recycling capacity of 400 kg / hr. of post Consumer and post commercial PP Plastic materials 
- Awareness raising (infographics) showing the results of the plastic study and benefits of a circular economy 

E-Waste: 
- Completed with UNU an e-waste statistics toolkit and the national e-waste assessment which includes recommendations for the sector
- Development of the recommendation report on how Lebanon can manage the e-waste. 

- Implementation phase: completed the technical support for the 2 beneficiaries:
Ecoserv: provide the needed equipment to enhance the e-waste collection through the NGO drop-off zones
Verdetech: improving their management system in order to improve their performance 

Stabilization Through Solid Waste Projects in Lebanon (Nafakhieh)
- Completed two technical analysis reports undertaken (including design and tender documents for landfill in Nafakhieh)
- Recruit project staff</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
