    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Solid Waste intervention in North Baalbeck: 
-Complete the construction of the MRF in Deir Al Ahmar;
-Complete of sorting at source awareness campaign and purchase of all needed collection equipment and bins;
-Complete the feasibility study of environmental technologies for plastic waste in Lebanon.

Plastic Waste:
- Complete the financial and economic assessment for the plastic sector in Lebanon;
-Identification of beneficiaries throughout the coordination with all stakeholders including the Ministry of Industry (MoI) and the Association of Lebanese Industries (ALI);
-Implementation phase: Upgrading recycling systems in Lebanese industries and NGOs; 
-Capacity building and awareness raising implemented to improve collection and sorting of plastic wastes;
-Call of Proposal for the support of 2 Municipalities is prepared.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Solid Waste intervention in North Baalbeck: 
- Completed the construction of the MRF in Deir Al Ahmar 
- Completed sorting at source awareness campaign and provision of bins (LOST)
- Procurement of five (5) pickup trucks with tipper body
- Completed the feasibility study of environmental technologies for plastic waste in Lebanon 
- Inauguaration of MRF in Deir Al Ahmar in the presence of Japanese embassy, Ministry of Envrionment and UNDP
 

Plastic Waste:
- Completing the Financial and economic assessment by consultant (Elard)
- The project is currently upgrading the existing recycling systems in 2 industries (GPI and 3MPlast) in order to increase the uptake of plastic recyclables. ?
- Prepared a report on circularity of plastics
- Commitment letters and targets set and signed by GPI and 3MPlast
- Support to the 2 NGOs (Live love Lebanon, and Recycle Lebanon has been completed


E-Waste:
- The project has completed the development of the needed questionnaire for data collection 
- The team has also completed the statistical survey on e-waste which will be used to produce inventory on the type and amount of e-waste generated in Lebanon.
- The project team has also identify the 2 main actors working on the E-waste sector. 2 site visits were conducted to their facility in order to assess the current situation. Based on the assessment, the project will be working on the technical support. 
Beneficiaries: Ecoserv: local NGO and Verdetech: private sector 

DRM: 
The project has drafted the ToRs for an external consultant to coordinate with various stakeholders to gather the data and assessments, identify cross cutting issues, set the priorities by sector, and synthesize the recommendations</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Solid Waste intervention in North Baalbeck:
- Complete the design and construction of the Material Recovery Facility (MRF) in Deir Al Ahmar 
-Implement awareness raising campaign on sorting at source in the selected villages with LOST
-Procure bins and refuse collection vehicles in coordination with LOST
-Conduct a feasibility study of environmental technologies for non-recyclable waste in Lebanon

Plastic Waste:
- prepare project document
- initiate the activities</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Solid Waste intervention in North Baalbeck:
After the completion of the awareness campaign on sorting at source in the selected villages, the project is currently procuring the needed trucks for the respective municipalities in order to enhance the waste collection. 
Five trucks will be provided as follows: three for the union of Deir Al Ahmar municipalities, one for Chlifa and one for Yammouneh.

The project has completed the data collection of the phase 4 of the plastic study, and is currently in the final stage of the assessment. The study has entered its final phase and is now assessing the general applicability of magneto pyrolysis treatment and its application in Lebanon. 

Based on bidding process that was conducted by the project team, a contracting company was awarded the MRF construction. Due to the COVID-19 pandemic and the security and economical country status, the work on site was significantly delayed; however, the team was able to undertake the project first phase and the construction work is expected to be completed by the end of June 2021.

Plastic Waste:
The team has initiated the financial and economic assessment for the plastic sector in Lebanon.
The project has identified the potential beneficiaries in the private sector for upgrading recycling systems in Lebanon. Currently the team is finalizing the evaluation.
In addition, the project has initiated the support for 2 NGOs for upgrading recycling systems. (including MoE, Association of Industries, etc.) to ensure the proper implementation of the project.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
